{
  "version": 3,
  "name": "dbx 160 VU",
  "category": "Dynamics",
  "author": "LiveWDF",
  "description": "dbx Model 160 hardware signal and control paths, with an LM308 substitution for the compensated op amps. The M1 macromodel uses the later THAT2180 Blackmer gain law with an output compliance clamp. The M2 detector reproduces true log-RMS and the specified 120 dB/s release, with a calibrated hard knee, continuous ratio and makeup gain. Input cold is grounded. Meter switching, bypass protection, trimmers and the mains regulator are outside the simulation.",
  "io": {
    "groundNode": "0",
    "inputNode": "in",
    "outputNode": "out"
  },
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "THRESH",
      "RATIO",
      "GAIN"
    ]
  },
